\doTocEntry\toclof{3}{\csname a:TocLink\endcsname{1}{x1-16005r3}{}{\ignorespaces Income and Consumption Growth. The growth of consumption for a consumer who stays employed falls as $m^{\mathrm@@ {e}}$ rises and equals income growth $\cc@accent {"7017}{\mathrm@@ {g}}$ at the target; its excess over the perfect foresight rate is the precautionary increment. Drawn by the handout's \href  {https://github.com/llorracc/TractableBufferStock/blob/main/TractableBufferStock.ipynb}{notebook}; run it in your browser, with nothing to install, in \href  {https://intertemporal-choice.github.io/lite/notebooks/index.html?path=TractableBufferStock.ipynb}{JupyterLite}, or open it in \href  {https://colab.research.google.com/github/llorracc/TractableBufferStock/blob/main/TractableBufferStock.ipynb}{Colab} or \href  {https://mybinder.org/v2/gh/intertemporal-choice/intertemporal-choice.github.io/main?labpath=content/consumption/TractableBufferStock/TractableBufferStock.ipynb}{Binder}.}}{figure}\relax 
